	(text "# LORA SUBSYSTEM DESIGN NOTES (LORA BLOCK)\nProject: OpenMycoNet BLE_BRIDGE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 2.3\n\nSYSTEM OVERVIEW\nThe LoRa subsystem provides long-range Sub-GHz wireless communication using an SX1262 transceiver (U9). It features an integrated LC\npower-amplifier bias feed, a Johanson matched balun (FL2), a PE4259 RF switch (U8) for Tx/Rx path multiplexing, and a coaxial antenna interface\n(J4). Communication and control are handled over the shared SPI bus and dedicated control signals connected to the ESP32-S3.\n\n1. TRANSCEIVER CORE AND POWER MANAGEMENT (U9 SX1262IMLTRT)\n• Core Transceiver: U9 (SX1262IMLTRT Sub-GHz LoRa/FSK transceiver).\n• Primary Supply Filtering: Main +3.3V digital supply rail filtered by FB1 ferrite bead to produce isolated 3V3_RF power rail, decoupled by \n  C22(10uF), C23 (100 nF), and C25 (47 uF).\n• Core Voltage Rails: Power pins VDD_IN (pin 10), VBAT (pin 3), and VBAT_IO (pin 11) powered directly from 3V3_RF rail.\n• Internal Regulators: VREG pin (pin 7) decoupled by C24 (470 nF) to GND. VR_PA pin (pin 24) decoupled by C27 (100 nF) to GND.\n• DC-DC Converter: Internal switching converter DCC_SW pin (pin 9) connected to L3 (15 uH power inductor) for high-efficiency power regulation.\n• Reference Clock: Y1 (32 MHz crystal unit) connected across XTA (pin 1) and XTB (pin 2).\n\n2. RF FRONT-END, BALUN, AND ANTENNA PATH\n• Power-Amp Bias Feed: RFO_TX pin (pin 23) powered via L4 (27 nH RF choke inductor) connected to the VR_PA rail.\n• Integrated Balun (FL2 0900FM15K0039): Converts differential RF_N (pin 22) and RF_P (pin 21) transceiver lines into a single-ended signal.\n• RF Switch (U8 PE4259): Multiplexes Tx and Rx paths to the antenna. Transmit path (RF1 PATH) and receive path (RF2 PATH) interface with U8, driven\n  by DIO2 control signal for automatic Tx/Rx switching.\n• Antenna Interface: Combined ANT line routes through DC-blocking capacitor C28 (47 pF) to coaxial connector J4 (Conn_Coaxial_Small).\n\n3. CONTROL LOGIC AND SPI BUS INTERFACE\n• Shared SPI Bus: Communicates via SPI.SPI_SCK (pin 18), SPI.SPI_MISO (pin 16), and SPI.SPI_MOSI (pin 17).\n• Chip Select Isolation: SPI.SPI_NSS pin (pin 19) pulled HIGH to +3.3V via R31 (10 kohm) resistor to ensure proper bus selection.\n• Hardware Reset: Active-LOW RESET pin (pin 15) driven by RESET_LoRa net from ESP32-S3 (IO7).\n• Status & Interrupt Lines: BUSY pin (pin 14) outputs BUSY_LoRa status to ESP32-S3 (IO10), DIO1 pin (pin 13) outputs DIO1 interrupts to ESP32-S3\n  (IO11), and DIO2 pin (pin 12) controls RF switch path.\n\n4. SUBSYSTEM INTERFACE MATRIX\n• SPI.SPI_NSS: Active-LOW chip select line (Pulled HIGH via R31 10 kohm).\n• SPI.SPI_SCK / MISO / MOSI: Shared hardware SPI bus lines connected to ESP32-S3.\n• RESET_LoRa: Transceiver hardware reset line driven by ESP32-S3 (IO7).\n• BUSY_LoRa: Transceiver busy status line output to ESP32-S3 (IO10).\n• DIO1: Interrupt request signal line output to ESP32-S3 (IO11).\n• J4: Coaxial antenna connector for external Sub-GHz antenna."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
